    [{:area "Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (solar PV)",
      :description
      "Version 2.0 explicitly states a Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (60%) for solar PV and includes a Supplier warranty in Representations & Warranties that the facility meets that Domestic Content Level. Version 3.1.1 removes the Minimum Required Domestic Content Level line item in Part 1.B(5)(iv) and the corresponding warranty in Part 2, Section 4.4.",
      :impact
      "Major — removes an explicit Supplier compliance obligation tied to domestic content. This may change eligibility or post-contract compliance exposure for Suppliers who had to meet domestic content thresholds; conversely, it may relieve Suppliers from that contractual warranty. Parties should confirm whether other Program rules or external statutes/regulations still impose domestic content requirements despite this deletion."}
     {:area
