    :summary
    "The two contracts are largely the same; the principal differences are (1) deletion in Version 3.1.1 of the explicit Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (60%) and the related Supplier warranty, and (2) expanded disclosure language in Version 3.1.1 that expressly allows sharing Facility details with other government ministries/agencies for public health/safety and emergency response. A minor procedural change requires notifications 'in the Prescribed Form' in Version 3.1.1. The domestic content deletion and broader data sharing are the most material changes — they respectively affect Supplier compliance obligations and increase privacy/exposure risk. Parties should verify whether regulatory rules outside the contract retain the domestic content requirement and should update privacy, notice and operational procedures to reflect the broader disclosure and the 'Prescribed Form' requirement."}},
